<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5911" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφικύπελλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> always <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέπας ἀ.</span></b> 
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>double cup,</i> such as forms a
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύπελλον</span> both at top and
			bottom, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.584
			</span></i>,al.: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφικύπελλα</span> are
			compared with the cell of a honeycomb, as possessing <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφίστομοι θυρίδες,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				624a9
			</span></i>; but acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i>, <i>two-handled,</i> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.783b
			</span></i> (post <i><span class="en">
				11.466c
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
